[
    {
        "content": "<p>To stress-test the tactic <code>inferInstanceAsPercent</code>, I've replaced throughout the library all<code>inferInstanceAs</code>with <code>inferInstanceAs%</code> because, after all, it's supposed to be a better replacement. This gives some interesting failures (see <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36151\">#36151</a>). One of the first ones is in <code>Data.Vector.Defs</code>.  On</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstanceAs</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">})</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>it gives the error</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">inferInstanceAs</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">head</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span>\n<span class=\"n\">does</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">head</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>where the universes are not forammly the same: for the first one it's <code>DecidableEq : Type (max 0 u_1) → Type (max 0 u_1)</code> and for the second one it's <code>DecidableEq : Type u_1 → Type u_1</code>.<br>\n<span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110087\">@Kim Morrison</span></p>",
        "id": 577336062,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1772651700
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Another example is</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableLT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DecidableLT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"bp\">ᵒᵈ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstanceAs</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableRel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>with error message</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">inferInstanceAs</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">head</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableRel</span>\n<span class=\"n\">does</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">head</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">DecidableLT</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 577348403,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1772655988
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110050\">Sébastien Gouëzel</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/inferInstanceAsPercent/near/577336062\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">inferInstanceAs</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">head</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span>\n<span class=\"n\">does</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">head</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>How do you fix this one? Even begging doesn't seem to work:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstanceAs</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(same error)</p>",
        "id": 577360252,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1772660459
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>explicit universes maybe?</p>",
        "id": 577360855,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1772660711
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>like doing <code>DecidableEq.{u}</code></p>",
        "id": 577360929,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1772660742
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I mentioned the messages just in case Kim wants to have a look to fix the tactic. I think we shouldn't fix the application at this specific place -- here, it would be enough to just use <code>inferInstanceAs</code> -- but rather make the tactic itself more robust.</p>",
        "id": 577361236,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1772660858
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Aha, <code>DecidableEq.{u+1}</code> does fix it.</p>",
        "id": 577366761,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1772662911
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(Breadcrumbs... <code>inferInstanceAs%</code> is in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/35950\">#35950</a>. Reviews and/or merging, even if in imperfect state, would make experimenting and improving easier!)</p>",
        "id": 577465288,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1772707144
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've merged it, with the understanding that this is partly a diagnostic tool and will help speed up progress.</p>",
        "id": 577467598,
        "sender_full_name": "Damiano Testa",
        "timestamp": 1772707783
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oops, I just pushed a fix that should solve the universe problem (there's a test case reflecting the Vector example above), which cancelled bors.</p>",
        "id": 577469499,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1772708377
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think we'll have to commit to moving this, or some alternative, up to <code>lean4</code> before we can release <code>v4.29.0</code>, as it seems an essential part of the fix. So it shouldn't be in Mathlib for too long.</p>",
        "id": 577469653,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1772708421
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Let's at least wait for CI :)</p>",
        "id": 577470587,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1772708679
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We should run radar to make sure <code>inferInstance%</code> isn't too slow (the implementation didn't look particularly fast to me, though maybe it's not used often enough for this to be significant)</p>",
        "id": 577471560,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1772708966
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've pushed what I think is a performance improvement... <code>!radar</code> says however that the slowdown in StandardPart is exactly the same, but now it says there is no overall change. <span aria-label=\"woman shrugging\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f937-200d-2640\" role=\"img\" title=\"woman shrugging\">:woman_shrugging:</span> </p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"479299\">@Jovan Gerbscheid</span>, do you have ideas for getting better performance here?</p>",
        "id": 577632730,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1772759912
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Testing the whole library with <code>inferInstanceAs%</code>in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36151\">#36151</a>, I get other interesting failures. For instance</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Error</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">CategoryTheory</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Pi</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lean</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">66</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstanceAs</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">head</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">J</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">v₁</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u₁</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"n\">does</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">head</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">J</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">v₁</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u₁</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∘</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 577663820,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1772779511
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>or</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Error</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">Homology</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">HasNoLoop</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lean</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">63</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"mi\">8</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstanceAs</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">head</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">HasNoLoop</span>\n<span class=\"n\">does</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">head</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">down'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">HasNoLoop</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 577663863,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1772779540
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110050\">@Sébastien Gouëzel</span>, its helpful if when doing things like this you reference either <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/35950\">#35950</a> (my <code>inferInstanceAs%</code>) or <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36420\">#36420</a> (<span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"479299\">@Jovan Gerbscheid</span>'s).</p>",
        "id": 579217748,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1773393581
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for doing these investigations, I've been looking at <code>inferInstanceAs%</code> (both versions!) again today, and managed (thanks for <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"873547\">@Robin Arnez</span>'s clever suggestion) got them running with <code>deriving</code>. Branches are still a bit of a mess, but I'll try and write a summary soon.</p>",
        "id": 579218373,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1773393763
    }
]